{
 "id": "d-exp",
 "course": "Calculus 1",
 "unit": "Derivatives",
 "title": "Derivatives of Exponentials",
 "subtitle": "The function that is its own derivative.",
 "version": 2,
 "graphs": {},
 "drills": {
  "theory": {
   "title": "Theory",
   "mode": "all",
   "questions": [
    {
     "id": "T1",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$frac{d}{dx} e^x =$",
     "options": [
      "$e^x$",
      "$xe^(x-1)$",
      "$e^(x-1)$",
      "$ln(x)$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "$e^x$ is its own derivative."
    },
    {
     "id": "T2",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$frac{d}{dx} e^(g(x)) =$",
     "options": [
      "$e^(g(x))·g'(x)$",
      "$e^(g'(x))$",
      "$g(x)e^(g(x)-1)$",
      "$e^(g(x))$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "Chain rule: the exponent stays, times its derivative."
    },
    {
     "id": "T3",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "$frac{d}{dx} b^x =$",
     "options": [
      "$b^x ln(b)$",
      "$xb^(x-1)$",
      "$b^x$",
      "$frac{b^x}{ln(b)}$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "Every base other than $e$ picks up $ln(b)$."
    },
    {
     "id": "T4",
     "type": "tf",
     "text": "$frac{d}{dx} e^(2x) = e^(2x)$",
     "answer": false,
     "explain": "$2e^(2x)$: multiply by the derivative of the exponent."
    },
    {
     "id": "T5",
     "type": "match",
     "text": "Match the exponent rules.",
     "pairs": [
      [
       "$a^x a^y$",
       "$a^(x+y)$"
      ],
      [
       "$frac{a^x}{a^y}$",
       "$a^(x-y)$"
      ],
      [
       "$(a^x)^y$",
       "$a^(xy)$"
      ],
      [
       "$a^(-x)$",
       "$frac{1}{a^x}$"
      ]
     ],
     "explain": "These let you simplify before you differentiate."
    },
    {
     "id": "T6",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "Which is the derivative of $x^e$ (a **power** of $x$, not an exponential)?",
     "options": [
      "$ex^(e-1)$",
      "$x^e$",
      "$e^x$",
      "$x^e ln(x)$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "$e$ is just a number (about 2.718), so the power rule applies."
    },
    {
     "id": "T7",
     "type": "mc",
     "text": "The number $e$ is chosen so that",
     "options": [
      "$lim[h->0] frac{e^h - 1}{h} = 1$",
      "$e^0 = e$",
      "$e = 3$",
      "$lim[h->0] e^h = 0$"
     ],
     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "That limit is the slope of $e^x$ at $x = 0$. Making it 1 makes $frac{d}{dx} e^x = e^x$."
    }
   ]
  },
